            "review_title": "Review at Mi Han Quoc",
            "review_text": "kaliboosh\n18 contributions\n0\nDecent food\nMar 2015 • Solo\nI just had the pork-covered rice, and it was decent. I knew not to expect good Korean food in Vietnam, so I wasn't very disappointed. \n\nThe restaurant had a ton of Vietnamese people for dinner and everyone else seemed to be having the Korean barbecue or the shabu-shabu, which is probably what the restaurant is known for. It smelled extremely good. I just went for the cheap and quick option to eat and leave so didn't bother ordering barbecue, but if you're ever craving for good meat, this seems like a good place to try.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 21, 2015",
